{
  "_comment": [
    "The Go modules linked into the bundled xray binary, and the Go toolchain that built it (MR-1685).",
    "scripts/generate-third-party-notices.mjs reads the modules, their versions and the Go version from the",
    "xray binary itself and FAILS unless each one is listed here with that exact version, a reviewed licence",
    "and its licence texts: an Xray bump cannot ship until the licences of what it links are vendored and read.",
    "Refresh with `node scripts/vendor-xray-go-licences.mjs <the four release xray binaries>`: it vendors",
    "every module's root LICENSE/COPYING/NOTICE files from proxy.golang.org into third_party/licenses/xray/",
    "<module>@<version>/ and Go's LICENSE for the toolchain, and sets `version` and `texts`. `license` (SPDX)",
    "and `source` are a person's job: a new module arrives as UNREVIEWED, which the generator refuses. GPL,",
    "LGPL and MPL modules need `source`; extra texts such as GPL-3.0.txt (paths under third_party/licenses/)",
    "are kept across refreshes.",
    "Every module also needs `zipSha256`: the SHA-256 of <module>@<version>.zip from proxy.golang.org, which",
    "every release mirrors in its corresponding-source asset (scripts/build-corresponding-source.mjs; owner decision",
    "2026-10-14 and review round 1: the GPL-3.0 binary's corresponding source covers every linked module) and",
    "refuses to publish if the downloaded zip differs. The vendor script records it for every module."
  ],
